# Aster v2 — Attribution

This project incorporates data, methods, and algorithmic references from the
following third-party sources. None impose copyleft or licensing obligations
on Aster v2's MIT-licensed source code.

## Lambert problem algorithm

- Algorithm: Izzo 2014, "Revisiting Lambert's Problem"
- Paper: arXiv:1403.2705 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1403.2705)
- Usage: Aster v2 implements Izzo's Lambert algorithm in TypeScript, drawing
  the mathematical formulation from the original paper. The implementation
  is clean-room (no vendored upstream source). See
  src/v2/core/lambert/ for the implementation when it lands.
- Validation reference: the poliastro project (https://github.com/poliastro/poliastro,
  MIT-licensed) provides high-quality test vectors that Aster v2's Lambert
  implementation must match within numerical tolerance.

## Tycho-2 star catalog

- Source: VizieR, ESO
- Component used: V_T <= 8.1 all-sky subset (40,000 stars) for visualization background
- Citation: Hog, E. et al. 2000, "The Tycho-2 Catalogue of the 2.5 Million Brightest Stars,"
  Astronomy & Astrophysics 355, L27
- Distribution: This subset is included in the Aster v2 repository at
  tests/fixtures/v2/star-catalog-tycho2-mag75.bin

## NEA catalog data

- Source: NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory, Small-Body Database (SBDB)
- URL: https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/sbdb_query.api
- Usage: NEA orbital elements ingested for the 41,906-body catalog.
  See Slice 9 founding doc for full ingestion methodology.

## Solar system body ephemerides

- Source: NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory, Horizons System
- URL: https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/
- Component used: Tabulated state vectors (position, velocity) for Sun, Mercury,
  Venus, Earth, Moon, Mars across 2026-2040 at daily cadence
- Distribution: tests/fixtures/v2/horizons-inner-solar-system-2026-2040.json
- Generator: tools/slice10-research/extend-horizons-fixture.mjs

## Historical reference: PyKEP vendor attempt (abandoned)

A vendoring attempt of PyKEP's C++ Lambert solver was investigated and
abandoned in favor of clean-room TypeScript implementation. See
src/v2/research/slice-10-lambert/pykep-vendor-attempt-postmortem.md
for the engineering record.
